{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["(Genesis 42:10–11) <b>And they said to him, No, my lord,</b> etc. 'We are all the sons of one man' — therefore we were afraid of the evil eye, which prevails all the more when one sees a number of handsome brothers in one place, more so than if each had been the son of a different man. And so our father commanded us, ״לָמָּה תִתְרָאוּ״ (Genesis 42:1), and from this we learned to hide ourselves among the arrivals. And if so, your servants are not spies, for every man is presumed respectable, and whoever wishes to remove him from his presumption bears the burden of proof. And since you have no other proof except our hiding among the arrivals — and behold, we are offering an explanation for this and you have no proof — consequently his charge of ״עֶרְוַת הָאָרֶץ בָּאתֶם לִרְאוֹת״ (Genesis 42:9) is also dismissed. And the brothers did not need to make this point explicitly, for Yosef himself conceded that the charge of ״עֶרְוַת הָאָרֶץ בָּאתֶם לִרְאוֹת״ depends on the charge of ״מְרַגְּלִים אַתֶּם״ (Genesis 42:9), and when the charge of 'you are spies' is dismissed, the charge about the exposed parts of the land is automatically dismissed as well."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "The lemma citation (י-יא) refers to verses 10–11, matching the bold heading and the opening words quoted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:00.099156234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}